      "index": 0,
      "text": "<think>\nTo find the product of 99 and 18, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts.\n\nFirst, I'll express 99 as (100 - 1). This allows me to use the distributive property effectively.\n\nNext, I'll multiply each term by 18. So, 100 multiplied by 18 is 1800, and 1 multiplied by 18 is 18.\n\nFinally, I'll add these two results together: 1800 plus 18 equals 1818.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **99** and **18**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   \n   - **99** can be written as **(100 - 1)**.\n   - **18** remains as it is.\n\n2. **Apply the Distributive Property:**\n   \n   \\[\n   99 \\times 18 = (100 - 1) \\times 18\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply Each Term:**\n   \n   \\[\n   = 100 \\times 18 - 1 \\times 18\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Calculate Each Part:**\n   \n   - \\(100 \\times 18 = 1800\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 18 = 18\\)\n   \n5. **Subtract the Results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1800 - 18 = 1782\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1782}\n\\]",
